{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++11 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cstring>\nusing namespace std;\ntypedef long long ll;\nconst int MOD = 1e9 + 7;\n\nusing Mat = vector<vector<ll>>;\n\nMat mul(const Mat& x, const Mat& y) {\n    int sz = x.size() - 1;\n    Mat z(sz + 1, vector<ll>(sz + 1, 0));\n    for (int i = 0; i <= sz; ++i)\n        for (int j = 0; j <= sz; ++j)\n            for (int k = 0; k <= sz; ++k)\n                z[i][j] = (z[i][j] + x[i][k] * y[k][j]) % MOD;\n    return z;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(0);\n    ll n, m;\n    cin >> n >> m;\n    ll tmp = n;\n    int cnt = -1;\n    ll dig[75];\n    while (tmp) {\n        dig[++cnt] = tmp % m;\n        tmp /= m;\n    }\n    vector<vector<Mat>> f(cnt + 1, vector<Mat>(m, Mat(m + 1, vector<ll>(m + 1, 0))));\n    Mat g(m + 1, vector<ll>(m + 1, 0));\n    g[0][m] = 1;\n    for (int j = 0; j < m; ++j) {\n        for (int i = 0; i <= m; ++i) {\n            f[0][j][i][j] = 1;\n            f[0][j][i][i] = 1;\n        }\n    }\n    for (int i = 1; i <= cnt; ++i) {\n        vector<Mat> pre(m), suf(m);\n        pre[0] = f[i-1][0];\n        for (int j = 1; j < m; ++j)\n            pre[j] = mul(pre[j-1], f[i-1][j]);\n        suf[m-1] = f[i-1][m-1];\n        for (int j = m-2; j >= 0; --j)\n            suf[j] = mul(f[i-1][j], suf[j+1]);\n        f[i][0] = suf[0];\n        for (int j = 1; j < m; ++j)\n            f[i][j] = mul(suf[j], pre[j-1]);\n    }\n    int cur = 0;\n    for (int i = cnt; i >= 0; --i) {\n        while (dig[i]--) {\n            g = mul(g, f[i][cur]);\n            cur = (cur + 1) % m;\n        }\n    }\n    ll ans = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i <= m; ++i)\n        ans = (ans + g[0][i]) % MOD;\n    cout << ans << '\\n';\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static final long MOD = 1000000007L;\n\n    static long[][] mul(long[][] x, long[][] y) {\n        int sz = x.length - 1;\n        long[][] z = new long[sz + 1][sz + 1];\n        for (int i = 0; i <= sz; i++) {\n            for (int j = 0; j <= sz; j++) {\n                long sum = 0;\n                for (int k = 0; k <= sz; k++) {\n                    sum = (sum + x[i][k] * y[k][j]) % MOD;\n                }\n                z[i][j] = sum;\n            }\n        }\n        return z;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        StringTokenizer st = new StringTokenizer(br.readLine());\n        long n = Long.parseLong(st.nextToken());\n        long m = Long.parseLong(st.nextToken());\n\n        long tmp = n;\n        int cnt = -1;\n        long[] dig = new long[75];\n        while (tmp > 0) {\n            dig[++cnt] = tmp % m;\n            tmp /= m;\n        }\n\n        // f[cnt+1][m][m+1][m+1]\n        long[][][][] f = new long[cnt + 1][(int) m][(int) (m + 1)][(int) (m + 1)];\n\n        // Initialize f[0]\n        for (int j = 0; j < m; j++) {\n            for (int i = 0; i <= m; i++) {\n                f[0][j][i][j] = 1;\n                f[0][j][i][i] = 1;\n            }\n        }\n\n        // Build f for higher positions\n        for (int i = 1; i <= cnt; i++) {\n            long[][][] pre = new long[(int) m][(int) (m + 1)][(int) (m + 1)];\n            long[][][] suf = new long[(int) m][(int) (m + 1)][(int) (m + 1)];\n\n            pre[0] = f[i - 1][0];\n            for (int j = 1; j < m; j++) {\n                pre[j] = mul(pre[j - 1], f[i - 1][j]);\n            }\n\n            suf[(int) m - 1] = f[i - 1][(int) m - 1];\n            for (int j = (int) m - 2; j >= 0; j--) {\n                suf[j] = mul(f[i - 1][j], suf[j + 1]);\n            }\n\n            f[i][0] = suf[0];\n            for (int j = 1; j < m; j++) {\n                f[i][j] = mul(suf[j], pre[j - 1]);\n            }\n        }\n\n        long[][] g = new long[(int) (m + 1)][(int) (m + 1)];\n        g[0][(int) m] = 1;\n\n        int cur = 0;\n        for (int i = cnt; i >= 0; i--) {\n            long times = dig[i];\n            for (long t = times; t > 0; t--) {\n                g = mul(g, f[i][cur]);\n                cur = (cur + 1) % (int) m;\n            }\n        }\n\n        long ans = 0;\n        for (int i = 0; i <= m; i++) {\n            ans = (ans + g[0][i]) % MOD;\n        }\n        System.out.println(ans);\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.98\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.4758453071117401, -0.00012420836719684303, 0.0, 0.0, -3.075552376685664e-05, -5.793403761344962e-05, 0.0, -0.004078404977917671, -0.10023580491542816, -3.576278118089249e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.0132738680113107e-05, -0.004249946679919958, -5.602820692729438e-06, 0.0, -3.576272320060525e-06, -0.0002076410164590925, -3.814689989667386e-06, -0.0619717612862587, -1.7881377516459906e-06, -2.264974000354414e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -7.390948667307384e-06, -0.0011701886542141438, -4.768370